# Binary — Prettier cannot format it and would corrupt it.
*.xlsx

# Markdown is DELIBERATELY excluded.
#
# CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF.md, PHASE-1-DISCOVERY.md and notes/ are hand-formatted
# documents, not code. Prettier reflows prose, rewrites list markers and
# re-wraps tables, which would produce an enormous diff on source-of-truth
# files and make their history unreadable — for no correctness benefit.
#
# Prettier formats code here. Prose stays the author's.
*.md

# .mdx too — case studies are prose, not code. Reflowing a case study's
# paragraphs would fight the author for the same reason it would in .md, and
# these files are the most carefully worded content on the site.
*.mdx

# .astro is DELIBERATELY excluded — prettier-plugin-astro is not idempotent.
#
# On four files (DeliveryThread, SiteHeader, ProjectCard, work/[...slug]),
# `prettier --write` reports "unchanged" while `prettier --check` simultaneously
# reports them as needing formatting. Verified across three consecutive passes:
# write and check disagree with each other. That is a plugin bug, and it would
# leave `npm run format:check` — and therefore CI — permanently red through no
# fault of the code.
#
# Correctness for .astro files is covered by ESLint via eslint-plugin-astro,
# which runs in CI and passes. Prettier formats .ts, .css, .json, .mjs and .js
# here. Revisit if the plugin stabilises.
*.astro
